---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import communitiesData from '@data/communities.json';
import { SOCIALS } from '../config';
import '@styles/practice.css';
const linkedin = SOCIALS.find(s => s.label === 'LinkedIn')!;
---
<Layout title="About Karan Mittal | Engineer-scientist" description="Karan Mittal is an engineer-scientist, Dextar co-founder, and community organiser focused on solving useful problems and building systems that last.">
  <main class="practice-page">
    <section class="hero"><div><span class="register">About / Karan Mittal</span><h1>An engineer-scientist, invested in the outcome.</h1><p class="lead">I like understanding difficult problems and building stable systems that actually solve them. The work matters when it makes an organisation more effective and leaves people with something they can rely on.</p></div><div class="hero-aside"><img class="hero-portrait" src="/profile-400.jpg" alt="Karan Mittal speaking at a technical event" width="180" height="216" /><span class="portrait-caption">Engineer, founder, educator, and community organiser.</span></div></section>
    <div class="reading"><section class="section"><h2>The problem comes before the tool.</h2><p>I’m co-founder of <a href="https://dextar.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dextar</a>. My experience spans enterprise knowledge infrastructure, life sciences, and finance. My current technical work includes knowledge retrieval, AI systems, and performance engineering.</p><p>I start by understanding the people, the workflow, and the constraints. Then I investigate what is happening, test possible explanations, and build around what the evidence supports. Sometimes that means better software. It can also mean a clearer decision, a simpler process, or helping a team understand the system it already has.</p><p>A successful handover matters to me: the team should understand what was built, why it works the way it does, and how to operate and improve it.</p><div class="actions"><a href="/work">Explore my work →</a><a href="/now">What I’m working on now →</a></div></section></div>
    <section class="section" id="community" aria-labelledby="community-title"><span class="register">Community & teaching</span><h2 id="community-title">Helping people build is part of the work.</h2><p class="lead">I organise, speak, and mentor in technical communities across Central India. Workshops and conversations give me a way to share what I understand, learn from others, and help engineers move from an idea to something they can build.</p>
      {communitiesData.communities.map(community => <article class="event-row"><img src={community.logo} alt="" width="48" height="48" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>{community.name}</h3><p>{community.description}</p><div class="actions">{community.links.map(link => <a href={link.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{link.label} ↗</a>)}</div></div></article>)}
      <div class="actions"><a href="/talks">Selected talks & workshops →</a><a href={linkedin.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">More events and activity on LinkedIn ↗</a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section closing"><h2>Bring a problem worth solving.</h2><p class="lead">I work with teams that need help understanding a difficult system, building a useful solution, or making progress through an uncertain technical decision.</p><a href="/contact" class="action">Discuss your problem →</a></section>
  </main>
</Layout>
